      "type": "LinguisticObject",
      "classified_as": [
        {
          "id": "aat:300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "pelt / peltry: an animal skin with the hair, wool or fur still attached, as traded raw or dressed by skinners and furriers; also peltry (peltria, peltry) for skins collectively, and old or low-quality skins. Specific skins are distinguished by the animal, treatment (raw, tanned, tawed), colour, origin and quality qualifiers below; named animal skins (rabbit, fox, lamb, marten, etc.) are catalogued under their own concepts."
    }
  ],
